{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/987428-practice-of-perfecting-and-crossover","id":987428,"title":"Practice of perfecting and crossover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-14T14:05:09-07:00","id":987428,"title":"Practice of perfecting and crossover","content":"So I am running a crossover group (yes,, I know this is a monkey's paw kind of scenario, but the players consist of my parents, siblings, and my sister's boyfriend, so it's much less formal) and an idea occurred to me. could a mage with 3 dots in an appropriate arcana use the practice of perfecting to empower other people's supernatural powers?. For instance, could a mage with 3 dots in Fate magic strengthen the contracts of a changeling? If so, any ideas how that would work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew thought process.<br /> &quot;I have this great idea for a power/splat/merit/etc/&quot;<br /> &quot;I have no idea if this is balanced, useless, or gamebreaking.&quot;<br /> &quot;I'll ask the internet&quot;<br /> &quot;The thread has died.&quot; <img src=\"images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4226-spiderlord","name":"Spiderlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:11:02-07:00","id":987432,"title":"","content":"Probably, because you can use Perfecting to strengthen ghosts n' spirits n' goetia and other gribblies. Maybe Fate 3 Perfecting could add Potency to Contract activation dicepools?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:16:57-07:00","id":987439,"title":"","content":"I say go for it, as long as it makes sense within the realm of your Chronicle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Huge fan of Crossover games myself. There's a lot of Mysteries to explore involving the other gamelines after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T19:14:19-07:00","id":988054,"title":"","content":"You should at most think about the effect of this in your game. Just think if you want the other splats to become more powerful by means of supernal buffs, or if this will be in your way. It seems perfectly reasonable by the rules, but sometimes crossovers need some thinkering with the rules.<br /> <br /> I find it much more extraordinary that you'l ST to your entire nuclear family and your sister's boyfriend...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T22:56:26-07:00","id":988142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spiderlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/987428-practice-of-perfecting-and-crossover#post987428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I am running a crossover group (yes,, I know this is a monkey's paw kind of scenario, but the players consist of my parents, siblings, and my sister's boyfriend, so it's much less formal) and an idea occurred to me. could a mage with 3 dots in an appropriate arcana use the practice of perfecting to empower other people's supernatural powers?. For instance, could a mage with 3 dots in Fate magic strengthen the contracts of a changeling? If so, any ideas how that would work?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the big things to consider here is that if you allow Mages to directly use the practice of Perfection on the powers of other supernaturals, are you going to be ok when they jump to the logical conclusion that the <i>other practices</i> (especially fraying, weakening them in an equal and opposite way of Perfecting) on them as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T23:01:13-07:00","id":988144,"title":"","content":"The mage is doing buffing anyway, and so is the changeling. The changeling's contract gives more dice for one action, but is harder to use. If the mage is going to be using her action for enhancing allies anyway, it makes sense to combine with the changeling to create an effect greater than either could achieve on their own, and it neatly deals with the problem of the mage having easier access to similar powers if they can make your powers easier. As for the composition of my group, my family is filled with RPG fans and I'm the one with the chronicles of darkness stuff, so I get to be the storyteller. My sister's boyfriend also likes RPGs and he hangs around the house often enough to be worth the effort of including, at least as an occasional group member.<br /> Edit<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the big things to consider here is that if you allow Mages to directly use the practice of Perfection on the powers of other supernaturals, are you going to be ok when they jump to the logical conclusion that the <i>other practices</i> (especially fraying, weakening them in an equal and opposite way of Perfecting) on them as well? </div> </div> </div>First of all, isn't there already a sidebar or something in the rulebook explicitly stating that the can use fraying as a counterspell for other supernatural powers? I seem to recall a note about dispelling werewolf gifts with a spirit 3 spell, but I could be wrong. second, the mage is being played by my mom, who has been playing RPGs since before I was born. I fully expect her (once she's had time to figure out the details of how arcana work) to do that, and I expect her to do it in such a way that it improves the game for everyone. She doesn't steal the spotlight from others constantly, which is why I felt confident letting her play the mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew thought process.<br /> &quot;I have this great idea for a power/splat/merit/etc/&quot;<br /> &quot;I have no idea if this is balanced, useless, or gamebreaking.&quot;<br /> &quot;I'll ask the internet&quot;<br /> &quot;The thread has died.&quot; <img src=\"images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","edited":{"userid":4226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4226-spiderlord","user":"Spiderlord","date":". 10-16-2016, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4226-spiderlord","name":"Spiderlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T23:39:22-07:00","id":988157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spiderlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/987428-practice-of-perfecting-and-crossover#post987428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">could a mage with 3 dots in an appropriate arcana use the practice of perfecting to empower other people's supernatural powers?. For instance, could a mage with 3 dots in Fate magic strengthen the contracts of a changeling? If so, any ideas how that would work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that answering &quot;yes&quot; implies that the same effects can be applied to Awakened spellcasting itself, take cues from the Yantra-boosters in Prime; don't add straight dice to power rolls outright, but feel free to give them 8- or 9-Again. Adding dice is best served by boosting the underlying mundane Traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T17:38:07-07:00","id":988532,"title":"","content":"I agree with Satchel, here. That's a good rule of thumb. Other sorts of relatively clean boosts could be things like &quot;adding one to the number of powers allowed of a given sort&quot; or, of course, straight attribute modifiers.<br /> <br /> Directly enhancing the extant powers of others is far more of a power-creep risk than allowing them to interact and bolster individual's ability. 1e Contracts could be manipulated by Fate effects, so feel free to allow that, but I think that was limited to rewriting them or slipping their leash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:27:10-07:00","id":994712,"title":"","content":"The specific contract I am hoping to modify is changeling fate (using the playtest for second edition). The changeling character dropped 3 of his five starting contract dots into this trick, but he can only use it on someone once per day. I was thinking that the mage could use 3 dot fate magic to overcome that limitation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew thought process.<br /> &quot;I have this great idea for a power/splat/merit/etc/&quot;<br /> &quot;I have no idea if this is balanced, useless, or gamebreaking.&quot;<br /> &quot;I'll ask the internet&quot;<br /> &quot;The thread has died.&quot; <img src=\"images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4226-spiderlord","name":"Spiderlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:44:22-07:00","id":994906,"title":"","content":"In that case, maybe let the changeling use it [Potency] times within the spell's duration. Or upgrade it to be used once per scene instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:30:01-07:00","id":994936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spiderlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/987428-practice-of-perfecting-and-crossover#post987428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I am running a crossover group (yes,, I know this is a monkey's paw kind of scenario, but the players consist of my parents, siblings, and my sister's boyfriend, so it's much less formal) and an idea occurred to me. could a mage with 3 dots in an appropriate arcana use the practice of perfecting to empower other people's supernatural powers?. For instance, could a mage with 3 dots in Fate magic strengthen the contracts of a changeling? If so, any ideas how that would work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my god that is the cutest. I wish my parents and siblings would play Mage with me.<br /> Aside from my sister, but we're almost twins the way we interact.<br /> <br /> And to answer your question: yes.<br /> <br /> It shouldn't necessarily be <i>easy,</i> but yes. Beasts can do something similar, you know, and everything under the sun is connected to the Supernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:43:34-07:00","id":994943,"title":"","content":"If it's a times per day limitation I'd use Time to fix it. Every day he doesn't use his power set up a Hung Spell to catch the contract power and relinquish control of the spell to him. He could only carry around like, 3 max, but it beats having it available only once.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, use Time to trick the contract into resetting.<br /> <br /> A Fate Patterning effect might be able to rewrite things about the contract though, so that could be a solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}